<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Finding integers for a logarithmic equation</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Solve the equation</p>
\[ \log_{{@b@}} (x + {@a@}) = \log_{{@b@}} (2x - {@c@}) + 1. \]
<p>\(x =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</p>
<div>[[feedback:prt1]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked solution</h3>
<p>Write \(1\) as a logarithm: \(1 = \log_{{@b@}} {@b@}\). Then the product law gives</p>
\[ \log_{{@b@}} (2x - {@c@}) + \log_{{@b@}} {@b@} = \log_{{@b@}} \big({@b@}(2x - {@c@})\big). \]
<p>Both sides are logarithms to base \({@b@}\), so the numbers inside are equal:</p>
\[ x + {@a@} = {@b@}(2x - {@c@}) = {@2*b@}x - {@b*c@} \]
\[ {@a@} + {@b*c@} = {@2*b@}x - x \quad\Longrightarrow\quad {@a+b*c@} = {@2*b-1@}x \quad\Longrightarrow\quad x = {@k@}. \]
<p>Check: \(x + {@a@} = {@k+a@} > 0\) and \(2x - {@c@} = {@2*k-c@} > 0\), so both logarithms are defined.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
